---
// The plum panel: the masterclass stands on its own, and for some people it's
// the first step toward deeper training. Deliberately self-contained — the
// page keeps its visitors (no links to other courses); the CTA goes to the
// register section below. Bridge / heading / body are slots so the
// heal-the-healer door can turn the same panel toward the person; the
// defaults are the professional door's lines.
---

<section class="we-masterclass" id="path">
  <div class="we-masterclass-inner">
    <p class="we-masterclass-bridge">
      <slot name="bridge">You can't hold this for someone else until you've let it work on you first.</slot>
    </p>
    <div class="we-eyebrow">Where this leads</div>
    <h2 class="we-masterclass-h2">
      <slot name="heading">The doorway to <em>the practitioner path.</em></slot>
    </h2>
    <p class="we-masterclass-body">
      <slot name="body">
        The masterclass stands on its own — come, take what's useful, bring it
        home to your work. For some people it also turns out to be a doorway:
        the first honest look at whether holding this work for others belongs in
        your future. These 100 minutes are the inexpensive way to find out — and
        if they're as far as you go, they'll still have earned their keep.
      </slot>
    </p>
    <!-- data-sd-price: PriceSync swaps the euro token for the visitor's market
         label after load. The token must stay in the site's euro-after copy
         style (44€) — that's what marketing-prices.ts matches. -->
    <div class="we-masterclass-detail" data-sd-price="masterclass">100 minutes · Live · 44€ · Replay included</div>
    <div class="we-masterclass-cta-wrap">
      <a href="#register" class="we-link-cta">
        Reserve your seat <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right"></i>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
